/* Initial variables */
section__
@title "Prologue — A Quiet Time"

playerName = "Eldan"
ringFound = false
ringName = ""
companion = ""
courage = 50
corruption = 0
gold = 5
hasSword = false
allies = []
pathMarked = false

"The hills of the Shirelands breathe slow and green. Stories sit in the hedgerows like sleeping birds."
"You are ${playerName}, a small presence in a wide world. A letter arrived yesterday, the ink smudged with a warning. A strange ember slipped like a secret into your pocket."

choice__
@target 2
@input playerName
"Tell me your name (or press continue with ${playerName}):"
__choice

choice__
@target 3
"Pocket the letter and walk toward the village green."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Green With a Secret"

"The letter's words are simple: *Watch the fire. Keep to your feet.* You can feel a weight in your coat; your fingers find something round and warm."

choice__
@target 4
@action ringFound = true; ringName = "Ember-Ring"; corruption = corruption + 1
"Examine the warm thing (it glows faintly)."
__choice

choice__
@target 5
"Ignore it for now and visit the market."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Market and Rumours"

"At market you hear a traveller whisper of a grey rider and a city of yellow ash. The world seems to tilt in the telling."

choice__
@target 6
@action companion = "Ranger"; allies.push("Ranger")
"Seek out the Ranger — a lean person with a map."
__choice

choice__
@target 7
@action companion = "Loresinger"; allies.push("Loresinger")
"Find the Loresinger by the fountain, who hums old star-songs."
__choice

choice__
@target 8
@action companion = "Stonehand"; allies.push("Stonehand")
"Visit the Stonehand at the smithy — strength and blunt honesty."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Ember's Name"

if__ (ringFound == true) {
"The Ember-Ring hums softly in your palm. It promises a brightness and a terrible warmth."
} else__ {
"There is nothing in your hand but the memory of warmth."
}

choice__
@target 9
@action hasSword = true; gold = gold - 3
"Buy a cheap blade at the smithy (-3 gold)."
__choice

choice__
@target 10
"Leave the market and go home to pack."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Blade and a Bargain"

if__ (gold < 0) {
"You cannot afford it. The smith laughs and slams the counter shut."
choice__
@target 10
"Leave empty-handed."
**choice
} else** {
"You leave with a blunt sword. It fits your hand like a promise."
choice__
@target 10
"Pack and leave at dawn."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "The Letter Again"

"Night sits like a slow animal. The letter's last line curls: *If it calls, you must bring it to the Deep Forge.*"

choice__
@target 11
@action pathMarked = true
"Set out at first light toward the Deep Forge."
__choice

choice__
@target 12
"Stay one more day and ask the Loresinger about the Deep Forge."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Loresinger's Tale"

"The Loresinger speaks of an ember-ring made to bind and to break. Their voice makes the room small and hushed."

choice__
@target 11
@action corruption = corruption + 1
"Leave with heavy knowledge."
__choice

choice__
@target 13
"Ask more questions (linger)."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Linger in the Light"

"As you linger, you learn a map piece: a river bends like a sleeping wolf and the road beneath it comes to a forgotten gate."

choice__
@target 11
"Take the map and set out."
__choice
__section

/* The Long Road begins */
section__
@title "Dawn — The Road Opens"

"Dawn finds you at the lane's edge. Your companion — ${companion} — joins you, boots soft on the grass. The road ahead breathes into hills and thinned forests."

choice__
@target 14
"Follow the main road."
__choice

choice__
@target 15
"Slip to a smaller path by the river."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Main Road — A Wagon Passes"

"A merchant's wagon clatters by, laden with jars. The driver warns of black banners seen at dusk."

choice__
@target 16
@action courage = courage + 5
"Trade for news and press onward."
__choice

choice__
@target 17
"Ignore the warnings and speed up."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "River Path — Quiet"

"The river sings truthlessly. A small boat tied to a post rocks. You can hide and rest."

choice__
@target 18
@action gold = gold + 2
"Search the banks; find some coin (+2 gold)."
__choice

choice__
@target 19
"Rest a while and continue."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "At the Ford"

"The ford looks shallow, but you catch shapes moving on the far bank—riders perhaps."

choice__
@target 20
@action corruption = corruption + 2
"Sneak across, clutching the Ember-Ring close if you have it."
__choice

choice__
@target 21
"Wait and watch the riders pass."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "If They Pass"

"They pass: cloaked, silent, like smoke on legs. One pauses and turns its head as if listening."

choice__
@target 22
@action courage = courage - 5
"A chill passes through you; move on quickly."
__choice

choice__
@target 23
@action corruption = corruption + 3
"The rider's glance lingers. You feel your name slipping."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Storm Gathering"

"Clouds pile like dark linen. The road forks. The map from the Loresinger points left; memory urges right."

choice__
@target 24
"Take the left — the map's way."
__choice

choice__
@target 25
"Take the right — trust your feet."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Left — A Broken Gate"

"The gate is half fallen. Moss climbs its stones. Inside you see the path to the Deep Forge—a whistle of heat far off."

choice__
@target 26
@action pathMarked = true
"Enter the ruins to search for signs."
__choice

choice__
@target 27
"Skirt the outside and call out."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Right — An Old Hermit"

"An old hermit tends a brazier. He offers bread if you answer a riddle."

choice__
@target 28
@action courage = courage + 2; gold = gold - 1
"Trade your coin for a meal and an old story (-1 gold)."
__choice

choice__
@target 29
"Decline and push onward."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Ruins — A Spark"

if__ (ringFound == true) {
"Within the ruins a circle of cold iron reacts with the Ember-Ring. A hidden door sighs open."
choice__
@target 30
@action corruption = corruption + 5
"Step toward the door."
**choice
} else** {
"The ruins are empty but for old echoes. Nothing answers you."
choice__
@target 29
"Leave the ruins and rejoin the road."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Brazier Stories"

"The hermit tells of the Deep Forge where rings are made and unmade. He warns, 'A ring that longs will hollow its bearer.'"

choice__
@target 30
"Head to the Forge with the hermit's blessing."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Down the Hidden Door"

"The door closes like a secret behind you. Stairs descend into iron and old song. The Ember-Ring pulses, and your name tastes different."

choice__
@target 31
"Descend into the Deep Ways."
__choice
__section

/* Deep Ways */
section__
@title "Into Stone — Deep Ways"

"The world contracts to the scent of damp stone. You feel the gravity of a thousand spent forges."

choice__
@target 32
"Light a torch and press on."
__choice

choice__
@target 33
"Move silently in case you are not alone."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Torchlight — Old Hammermarks"

"Hammermarks tell of hands long gone. A chest sits wedged among the stones."

choice__
@target 34
@action gold = gold + 10
"Prise it open (find 10 gold)."
__choice

choice__
@target 35
"Leave it; treasure can be a snare."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Silent Steps"

"You hear a far chant, a voice threaded with iron. It speaks a name you do not know but which makes the Ember-Ring stir."

choice__
@target 36
@action corruption = corruption + 4
"Answer the chant."
__choice

choice__
@target 37
"Cover your ears and run."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Hidden Hoard"

"Inside the chest are old coins and a small, sturdy blade. It feels like it was waiting."

choice__
@target 38
@action hasSword = true; gold = gold + 2
"Take the blade and coin (+2 gold)."
__choice

choice__
@target 35
"Take nothing and move on."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Chant's Answer"

"The voice replies with a rustle of pages and a name: *Ashen Lord.* The name tastes like iron and smoke."

choice__
@target 39
"Mark the name and continue deeper."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Running — A Narrow Escape"

"You find a cascade of water that leads you to a side passage. For a while you forget the Ember-Ring's hum."

choice__
@target 40
"Follow the water."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Map Fragment"

"Behind a loose stone you find a map fragment showing a path beneath a river—an old way to the Fallen City."

choice__
@target 41
@action pathMarked = true
"Take the fragment."
__choice

choice__
@target 40
"Ignore it and press on."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Cold Chamber"

"In a chamber of iron you see a forge long cold. There, a pedestal waits for a ring."

if__ (ringFound == true) {
"The Ember-Ring throbs like a heartbeat. The pedestal seems to draw it."
choice__
@target 42
@action corruption = corruption + 10
"Place the ring on the pedestal."
__choice

```
choice__
  @target 43
  "Resist the pull and carry on."
__choice
```

} else__ {
"The pedestal is empty, but heat stains are clear. Someone came here to make or unmake."
choice__
@target 43
"Move on."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Placed — A Price"

"As you place the ring it surges. Visions like quick sparks—crowds, crowns, a city of ash—flash. When you snap the ring away, a fissure runs across the stone under your feet."

choice__
@target 44
"Flee the chamber."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Resisted — A Whisper"

"A whisper follows you: *You might have given so much.* Your fingers feel cold without the ring near them."

choice__
@target 44
"Keep walking, heedless."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "By the Underground River"

"The underground river is black and loudly sure. A small boat rests in a cleft."

choice__
@target 45
"Use the boat to cross."
__choice

choice__
@target 46
"Swim the river (dangerous)."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Boat — Across and Quiet"

"You cross slowly. On the far bank, a rusted gate stands, and beyond it the Fallen City's spires scrape the low roof of the world."

choice__
@target 47
"Approach the Fallen City."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Swim — A Fight"

"The current bites. You fight, and nearly lose the ring when something claws your ankle. You drag yourself out, breathless and changed."

choice__
@target 47
@action corruption = corruption + 5; courage = courage - 3
"Soaked, you press to the city."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "At the Fallen Gate"

"The city's gate is jagged, like a wound. Shadows live in its teeth. Somewhere beyond, a bell tolls once every hour."

choice__
@target 48
"Enter through the main gate."
__choice

choice__
@target 49
"Find a side entrance."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Main Gate — A Watcher"

"A watcher made of rust and old armor leans against the gate. It does not ask for a password. It asks for a name."

choice__
@target 50
@input playerName
"Speak your name to the watcher:"
__choice

choice__
@target 51
"Try to slip past when it dozes."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Side Entrance — Silent Steps"

"You slip through a collapsed aqueduct and find an inner street that smells of coal and lost things."

choice__
@target 52
"Move carefully toward the bell tower."
__choice
__section

/* The Fallen City scenes */
section__
@title "Inner Street — Market of Shadows"

"Shadows trade whispers here like they were coins. A figure in green offers you a chance: take the Ember-Ring to the forges, or keep it and seek power."

if__ (ringFound == true) {
choice__
@target 53
@action corruption = corruption - 5
"Hand the ring to the green figure (trust and hope)."
__choice

```
choice__
  @target 54
  @action corruption = corruption + 10
  "Refuse and keep the ring (fear and craving)."
__choice
```

} else__ {
"You have nothing they want. The green one vanishes like a thought."
choice__
@target 54
"Continue inward."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "The Green One's Choice"

"If you gave the ring away, you feel a peace like the end of a long cough. If you kept it, the green one's eyes nearly go out, but you feel a strength like a new callus."

if__ (ringFound == true) {
if__ (corruption <= 5) {
"Your heart feels light as you walk toward the tower of the bell."
choice__
@target 55
"Climb toward the bell tower."
**choice
} else** {
"You carry a weight that draws many eyes. The bell tower's shadow seems to seek you."
choice__
@target 56
"Push to the tower despite the eyes."
**choice
}
} else** {
choice__
@target 56
"Move toward the bell tower."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Bell Tower — A Toll"

"The bell rings with each step closer, and you feel the city's memory pressing outward."

choice__
@target 57
"Climb to the bell room."
__choice

choice__
@target 58
"Explore the houses below for allies."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Bell Room — An Old Script"

"In the bell room you find a scrawl: *Break the Ember where fire first sang.* A skylight overlooks a distant mountain crowned with steam."

choice__
@target 59
@action pathMarked = true
"Set course for the smoking peak."
__choice

choice__
@target 60
"Double back to gather more company."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Houses — Strange Allies"

"In the houses you find others: a veteran from a distant watch, a servant of an old order, and a child who keeps a small mirror."

choice__
@target 61
@action allies.push("Veteran"); allies.push("Servant"); allies.push("Child"); courage = courage + 5
"Recruit them to your company."
__choice

choice__
@target 61
"Leave and continue alone."
__choice
__section

/* Shadowmarch */
section__
@title "Crossing the Wastes"

"The road to the smoking peak crosses a waste of grey rock. Scattered bones make a map of sorrow. As you walk, the Ember-Ring grows warm and eager."

choice__
@target 62
"Walk openly and fast."
__choice

choice__
@target 63
"Move by the cover of night."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Open March — A Thunder of Wing"

"Wings beat overhead. Shadow-forms pass, listening for the ember's call. Your courage is tested."

choice__
@target 64
@action courage = courage + 10
"Stand and face them, shout a challenge."
__choice

choice__
@target 65
@action corruption = corruption + 5
"Hide the ring deeper in your coat and run."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Night March — A Quiet Theft"

"Under night the wasteland seems less cruel. You slip past a watching group, but something takes a step in your shadow and whispers your name."

choice__
@target 66
"Hush it with song."
__choice

choice__
@target 67
@action corruption = corruption + 3
"Feed it a thought you would rather not own."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "A Stand — Steel and Light"

"You meet them: shapes in old steel. The Ranger at your side draws a long bow; the Loresinger hums a note that brightens your sword."

choice__
@target 68
@action courage = courage + 5; corruption = corruption + 1
"Fight with them."
__choice

choice__
@target 69
"Surrender and bargain."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Run — The Chase"

"You run. The land stretches like a field of knives. For a while the Ember-Ring seems like a small, hot secret you could forget—but the riders do not forget."

choice__
@target 70
"Head to a ruined watchtower for refuge."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Song — A Calm"

"Your song soothes the shadow that followed. It leaves as if repelled by truth."

choice__
@target 68
"Join the fight refreshed."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Bargain — A Price Named"

"You try to bargain. The riders laugh as a bell tolls somewhere. 'Bring us the Ember or your friends,' they say."

choice__
@target 71
@action corruption = corruption + 10
"Promise them a lie to save your friends."
__choice

choice__
@target 72
"Refuse and stand by your companions."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Watchtower — High Ground"

"From the watchtower you see the smoking mountain like a black tooth. Fires ring its crown."

choice__
@target 73
"Rest, plan, and continue at first light."
__choice

choice__
@target 74
"Signal to any allies you recruited."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "The Riders' Demand"

if__ (corruption >= 20) {
"The lie you told spreads like shadow. It changes the look in your allies' eyes."
choice__
@target 75
"Push on despite the cost."
**choice
} else** {
"Your refusal steels your companions. They rally nearer."
choice__
@target 76
"Gather strength and press to the mountain."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Gathering — Old Oaths"

"By morning your small company swears old oaths. The Veteran tells you of a route that skirts the mountain's east, along an ancient pipe."

choice__
@target 77
"Take the Veteran's route."
__choice

choice__
@target 78
"Blaze your own trail toward the forge."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Pipe Route — A Narrow Pass"

"The pipe-route is cramped and quiet, but booby-trapped by time. You navigate with the Loresinger's notes."

choice__
@target 79
"Move slowly, watch every step."
__choice

choice__
@target 80
@action courage = courage - 5
"Rush—the quicker the less likely to be trapped."
__choice
__section

/* The Last Path scenes */
section__
@title "The Smelting Ridge"

"The ridge breathes sulphur. Heat scars the sky. At the ridge's head you see a furnace whose mouth is a black sun."

choice__
@target 81
"Approach the furnace's rim."
__choice

choice__
@target 82
"Search the gullies for a safer path."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Rim of the Furnace"

"The Ember-Ring sings like an answered bell. The forges remember all rings ever made."

if__ (ringFound == true) {
choice__
@target 83
@action corruption = corruption + 20
"Step onto the rim and speak a name used by no one else."
__choice

```
choice__
  @target 84
  "Look for a way to lower the Ember into the fire without stepping into it."
__choice
```

} else__ {
"You see tools and the mark of the old forgemasters. The rim is empty yet terrible."
choice__
@target 84
"Search for the masterwork."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Gullies — Hidden Path"

"A narrow path winds down where coals fall like slow rain. The Veteran remarks that only those hardened by grief can take it."

choice__
@target 85
"Take the hidden path."
__choice

choice__
@target 86
"Return to the rim, face the black sun."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "On the Rim — A Name Spoken"

"You whisper a name into the heat. The ring answers with visions: crowns crumbling, friends stilled, a throne of embers."

choice__
@target 87
"Take the ring and leap into the fire—end it."
__choice

choice__
@target 88
"Draw back; perhaps there is another way."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Lowering the Ember"

"You fashion a chain from old tools. With careful hands you lower the Ember-Ring toward the heart of the furnace."

choice__
@target 89
@action corruption = corruption - 15; ringFound = false; ringName = ""
"Let it fall and watch the fire drink it."
__choice

choice__
@target 90
@action corruption = corruption + 10
"Withdraw the Ember at the last moment—fear keeps you."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Hidden Path — The Sacrifice"

"The hidden path brings you to a small antechamber where old forgemasters wrote names in ash."

choice__
@target 91
"Write your name and the Ember's name together, then burn the paper in your palm as a vow."
__choice

choice__
@target 92
"Walk on; vows are luxuries when fire waits."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Leap — A Sudden End"

"You leap. Fire takes you as if you were a moth who had learned how to fly the wrong way. The story narrows."

choice__
@target 93
"—"
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Recoil — A Second Chance"

"You pull back. The Ember grows colder at your hesitation. Around you, shouts: someone has noticed your attempt."

choice__
@target 94
"Prepare to fight for the Ember."
__choice

choice__
@target 95
"Run with it—perhaps you can hide again."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Letting It Fall — The World Breathes"

"You let the Ember-Ring fall. It is sucked into the heart of the furnace with a scream of bright ash. A silence comes down like rain."

choice__
@target 96
"Feel the change as the ember's weight lifts."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Withdrawn — A Curse and a Burden"

"Withdrawing the Ember brings a howl. The mountain's old wards shudder, and from below a deep voice says, 'You will carry what you choose.'"

choice__
@target 97
"Accept the curse and wear it like armor."
__choice

choice__
@target 98
"Seek a wiser hand to take it from you."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Vow in Ash"

"You write names and burn them. The ash smells like memory. Something loosens in your heart; perhaps a small freedom has been bought."

choice__
@target 96
"Return to the rim and watch the fire."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "March of the Watchers"

"Whether you burned the paper or leapt or fled, the watchers come—armies of rust and shadow marching with a single purpose."

choice__
@target 99
"Stand and meet them as one."
__choice

choice__
@target 100
"Slip away through a forgotten sewer."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Stand — A Last Defense"

"You hold fast. Your companions form a ring about you. The battle is narrow and terrible, and some faces fall under the ash-sky."

if__ (courage >= 60) {
choice__
@target 101
"You push through with ferocity; the watchers break."
**choice
} else** {
choice__
@target 102
"You fight bravely, but the line cracks."
__choice
}
__section

section__
@title "Sewer — A Hidden Escape"

"In the sewer the air tastes like salt and old stories. The city coughs behind you, and a new horizon opens like a promise."

choice__
@target 103
"Follow the sewer to a distant shore."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Victory — The Breaking"

"Against the watchers you find a reserve of tired strength. The Ember's influence wanes as allies hold one another. The watchers fall and rust into the road."

choice__
@target 104
"Tend the wounded and speak your name aloud."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Crack — A Cost"

"The line cracks. You fall into a dream of iron and hunger. When you wake, part of your company is gone."

choice__
@target 105
"Mourn and keep moving."
__choice
__section

/* Endings and final choices */
section__
@title "Shores — A Quiet Morning"

"You stand where water meets black sand. The mountain smolders far behind. The Ember-Ring is gone or heavy in your pocket, depending on choices made."

if__ (ringFound == false) {
"There is a strange lightness to your step. The wind carries no whisper of a hidden throne."
} else__ {
"The Ember-Ring hums still. Its presence is a weight your bones remember."
}

choice__
@target 106
"Return home to the Shirelands and try to be small again."
__choice

choice__
@target 107
"Walk into the world and offer help where it is needed."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Tend the Wounded"

"You wash blood from hands that once helped you. Your companions still live because you chose to stay."

choice__
@target 108
"Settle near the shore and heal."
__choice

choice__
@target 109
"Press onward to find what other fires remain."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Mourn — A Hard Lesson"

"Loss teaches you a kind of patience. You carry names like small stones in your pocket."

choice__
@target 110
"Use your loss as a lantern, not a shackle."
__choice

choice__
@target 111
"Hide away—let the world forget your name."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Home — The Slow Returning"

"Back in the Shirelands the hedgerows seem unchanged; the people sip tea and tell easy tales. But when you reach for a coin or a sleeping child's hand, you know nothing is quite the same."

choice__
@target 112
"Live plainly; tell your story to no one."
__choice

choice__
@target 113
"Teach the young how to keep their feet steady."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Out in the World — A New Road"

"You travel to towns that once burned, carrying help or counsel. People remember and look to you as one who chose."

choice__
@target 114
"Found a small guild to help refugees."
__choice

choice__
@target 115
"Seek the old scholars to learn more of embers and rings."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Settle — Peaceful Ending"

"You build a quiet life by the shore, planting roots among survivors. Your days are soft; your nights sometimes haunted by the cold hum that used to be a ring."

choice__
@target 116
"Live out your days, content."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Press On — The Unfinished Road"

"You continue: there are still forges, and other ember-things. Your journey becomes a life of walking and decision."

choice__
@target 117
"Become a walker between places, a steady hand."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Use Loss as Lantern"

"Your grief lights your choices. You act to prevent others from losing what you lost."

choice__
@target 114
"Join those who rebuild."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Hide — A Quiet Decay"

"You hide, and the world forgets you, as you wished. But forgetting is a slow, dull sorrow."

choice__
@target 116
"Live quietly, letting the world close its doors."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Guild Founder"

"Your guild grows from a handful of tents to a steady hall. Children learn to mend bones and sew courage."

choice__
@target 118
"Name the guild and set down a charter."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Scholar's Road"

"Among dusty books you learn of many embers: small, faint and dangerous. You become part of a slow watch."

choice__
@target 119
"Record what you learned for those who will need it."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "End — Simple Life"

"Years pass. You tend a garden and sometimes dream of a grey rider's glance. Those dreams fade; your hands grow steady."

choice__
@target 120
"Close your story with a simple pen stroke."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Walker — The Quiet Road"

"You become a remembered name along the roads: a hand that helped, a voice that warned. You never again felt the Ember's pulse."

choice__
@target 120
"Your final scene: a path receding into light."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Guild — A Charter"

"You write rules that value small kindnesses and stern courage. The charter is read to apprentices; it keeps the worst at bay."

choice__
@target 120
"Pass on the charter and step back."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Record — Memory for Others"

"The scholar in you writes the Ember's tale cleanly. You leave it in a sealed codex, to be read when necessary."

choice__
@target 120
"Seal the codex and send it to the vaults."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Final Line"

"The road does not end so much as fork into many quieter trails. You chose a way—burned, fought, or resisted—and the world remembers in small, durable ways."

if__ (corruption >= 30) {
"There is a sadness in the epilogue: power leaves marks even when they are hidden."
} else__ {
"There is a lightness in the epilogue: what was nearly lost was sometimes saved by thin, brave hands."
}

"Thank you for walking this long road."

choice__
@target 1
"Restart the tale."
__choice

choice__
@target 120
"End here."
__choice
__section

/* Minimal epilog sections to complete 120 sections numbering */
section__
@title "Epilogue — The Map"
"A map hangs in a tavern, lines inked by hands who remember you. Some mention you kindly; some do not."
choice__
@target 120
"Fold the map and keep walking."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Bell"
"In a distant town a bell tolls once for those who gave and once for those who could not."
choice__
@target 120
"Listen and go on."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Child"
"A child looks at you with old eyes and asks if it's true a ring could change a person. You smile, remembering the price paid."
choice__
@target 120
"Teach them a small truth and move on."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Veteran"
"The Veteran keeps a scar as a reminder of what standing together can do."
choice__
@target 120
"Share a drink and keep telling that story."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Smith"
"In the smithy the blade you bought is used to cut bread and to build plows; it does ordinary good."
choice__
@target 120
"Lay down your tools at day's end."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Loresinger"
"The Loresinger's songs still soften the edges of a hard day; you hum one, and the world eases."
choice__
@target 120
"Hum and keep walking."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Stonehand"
"Stonehand keeps the old stones steady. You rest upon one and breathe."
choice__
@target 120
"Breathe and sleep."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Sea"
"Waves keep time with a patience older than kings. You watch them, and in the watching you feel small and whole."
choice__
@target 120
"Let the horizon hold you for a while."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The Codex"
"In a vault sealed with quiet, the codex on embers waits for future hands that need warning more than wonder."
choice__
@target 120
"Leave it there."
__choice
__section

section__
@title "Epilogue — The End"
"This, finally, is one of many endings. The road will always have more feet upon it. That is how stories live."
choice__
@target 1
"Begin again."
__choice

choice__
@target 120
"Close the book."
__choice
__section

/* End of file */
